<title>USA: Election lifts Medtronic, others.</title>
<headline>Election lifts Medtronic, others.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Medtronic Inc, Boston Scientific Corp, Target Therapeutics Inc, Johnson &amp; Johnson and other medical technology firms rose Wednedsay on Tuesday's election results, analysts said.</p>
<p>Retention by the Republicans of control of Congress was seen as positive for the sector in two ways.</p>
<p>First, it reduces the likelihood that President Clinton will be able to mount or push through any healthcare reform proposal that could cut profit margins or otherwise hurt medical technology, healthcare and drug firms, analysts said.</p>
</text>
